AI Personal Assistant (Multi-Agent System)
Overview

An AI-powered multi-agent personal assistant built with n8n that manages Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Tasks, and web research through a single Telegram chat interface.

Instead of relying on one AI agent to perform every task, the system uses an intelligent orchestrator that understands the user's request and delegates it to specialized agents responsible for individual services.

Problem

Managing productivity across multiple applications often requires users to switch between Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Tasks, and search engines just to complete simple tasks. This constant context switching reduces productivity and creates unnecessary friction.

Traditional AI assistants also struggle because one agent is responsible for every task, making the system harder to scale and maintain as new capabilities are added.

Solution

This project implements a modular multi-agent architecture where a central Orchestrator Agent acts as the decision maker.

When a user sends a request through Telegram, the orchestrator determines the user's intent and routes the request to the appropriate specialized agent.

Specialized agents include:

Gmail Agent
Google Calendar Agent
Google Tasks Agent
Web Research Agent

Each agent performs its task independently before returning the result to the orchestrator, which delivers the final response back to the user.

This architecture makes the system modular, scalable, and easy to extend with additional agents.

Outcome

The assistant enables users to manage multiple productivity tools from a single conversational interface.

Benefits include:

Eliminates the need to switch between multiple applications
Simplifies task and calendar management
Provides instant AI-powered web research
Modular architecture that supports future expansion
Faster execution of everyday productivity tasks
Demonstrates a scalable approach to building production-style AI agent systems

